{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Landed as Gerrit change 3111 (commit 47e431de04a, LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved, no advisories). make verify before the push: 17 failed, 19746 passed; all 17 failures are the known pandoc set under tests/unit/reconciler, none elsewhere, 0 ERROR lines.\n\nReproduction before the fix (2026-10-25, real git, two repos): origin/tickets held a commit the tracker lacked and the throttle marker was stamped 5 s ago. relation_snapshot.tracker_head_sha returned the tracker's old head, behind origin, and made no fetch.\n\nFix: ensure_fresh gains force, which skips only the 60 s age check; the opt-outs, the marker write and the swallow-every-failure contract are unchanged. force_fresh is threaded through tracker_head_sha, collect_plan_relation_snapshot and generation.collect, and set at the review-start snapshot and the pre-lock collect in sign_manifest only. The under-lock re-collect keeps the throttle, so nothing fetches while the lock is held.\n\nEvidence on the merged tree (HEAD 47e431de04a), 2026-10-25 10:50 PDT:\n- pytest tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py tests/unit/test_plan_relation_snapshot.py -q -> '40 passed in 108.52s'\n- pytest tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py -q -k 'forced or sign_manifest or review_start' -> '7 passed in 7.92s'\nAll 7 of those new tests failed before the fix, each for the intended reason: TypeError on the missing force_fresh keyword, and the sign_manifest refusal test reached signing on a superseded description. They cover: forced head read fetches inside the window while the default does not; the sync.pull opt-out still blocks a forced read; a failing fetch is swallowed and the local head is returned; a forced snapshot pins the description edited on origin; sign_manifest raises PlanReviewGenerationChanged inside the window with one fetch; a forced retry fetches once per attempt (2 attempts, 2 fetches) and none under the lock; review start passes force_fresh=True.\n\nDisposition: a forced fetch that fails is swallowed and review and signing continue on the local clone, as with the sync.pull opt-out. Unverified: end-to-end behavior on the deployed MCP server (two real clones); the tests use a two-repo fixture. Out of scope and ticketed as fabulous-avian-hoverfly: the claim-time currency check, which can still read a lagging clone."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792950664033114001,"uuid":"950f6c2e-2d79-46fe-86a6-46988042d957"}